guamp: invalidate the CPU view of surfaces the GPU wrote (AdrenoMetal 2ff4be9, NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm)

flushSurfaces only cleans (DC CVAC) and skips surfaces whose seed did not move, so a process reading a GPU-written
IOSurface (screenshot, app snapshot) could see stale cache lines. Render-pass targets are cleaned+invalidated (DC CIVAC)
at commit and after completion, for their first NMB_SURFACE_INVALIDATE (default 4) completed writes. Applied by the
guamp-kernel-build GPU user-space workflow (device/patches/adreno-metal/*.patch) when adreno_metal_ref is 2ff4be9.

